  placementText: {fileID: 8773322589981808993}
  displayDrawing1: {fileID: 2037472510}
  blockTitle: 'AT203: Geison'
  blockDescription: This block is part of the horizontal geison block. It bears cuttings
    for the rafters of the roof on the upper surface at a spacing of 55 cm, lion-head
    water spouts on the overhang, and sculptural decoration in the underside of the
    overhang, including modillions and sculptural cassettes with exceptional iconographic
    motifs, a turtle and an axe, interpreted as deriving from local precedents, as
    early as Hittite!
  blockPlacement: Found in the southwest quadrant, about 12 m. from its place on
    the temple. It is restored as part of the horizontal geison course on the right
    flank of the temple, adjacent to AT204.
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 0}
