  descriptionText: {fileID: 6213780209972709613}
  placementText: {fileID: 8773322589981808993}
  displayDrawing1: {fileID: 2037472510}
  blockTitle: 'AT638: Podium Base Molding'
  blockDescription: Unfinished podium base molding. Its slanted side would be carved
    down at the final stages, to give a molding with an ovolo, cyma and tainia. The
    molding turns in a U-shape, thus the block has to be restored at the front end
    of the podium by the stairs. This is the only piece of evidence that gives us
    the width of the front end of the podium.
  blockPlacement: Was found about 20 m. southwest of the temple, and it is restored
    at the right front corner of the podium.
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 3361ab2bd3223c84fbafb92beec435bf, type: 3}
