  blockTitle: 'AT173: Corinthian Column Capital '
  blockDescription: 'Block Description:

    Column capital, the best preserved of
    the four original ones. The capital is of the corinthian genus, bearing stylized
    acanthus leaves and tendrils in the corners and the middle part of the capital.
    The corinthian order was commonly used in Imperial Roman Architecture, as the
    most ornate order. '
  blockPlacement: Found in the SW quadrant.
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 0}
