  placementText: {fileID: 8773322589981808993}
  displayDrawing1: {fileID: 2037472510}
  blockTitle: 'AT186: Corner Frieze Block'
  blockDescription: The frieze course succeeded the architrave, and was underneath
    the roof cornice (geison). Aesthetically, this course provided a surface for
    decoration, which in this case included a cyma profile and a dentil course. Functionally,
    this course at the back face included cuttings for the support of the  joists
    of the roof.
  blockPlacement: "This is a corner frieze block, found to the southwest of the temple,
    and tbus is restored at the at the righthand corner of the temple front fa\xE7ade."
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7170c92e366a9e0468076602936e3123, type: 3}
